      "updated": 1775881265793,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "LLM guardrails are safety frameworks and control\nmechanisms that sit between a user and a Large\nLanguage Model to ensure outputs are reliable,\nsecure, and ethical. They act as filters to prevent\nharmful content, mitigate hallucinations, stop data\nleakage, and block prompt injection attacks. Common\ntypes include input filtering (screening prompts) and\noutput monitoring (checking responses).",
      "fontSize": 17.608432942792742,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "LLM guardrails are safety frameworks and control mechanisms that sit between a user and a Large Language Model to ensure outputs are reliable, secure, and ethical. They act as filters to prevent harmful content, mitigate hallucinations, stop data leakage, and block prompt injection attacks. Common types include input filtering (screening prompts) and output monitoring (checking responses).",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
